# UI design system

## Tokens

- Use tokens only: `AppTheme.colors`, `AppTheme.typography`, `AppTheme.spacing`, `AppTheme.radius`, `AppTheme.border`, `AppTheme.sizes`.
- Never write `Color(0x…)` or raw `N.dp` / `N.sp` literals outside `core/designsystem/theme/`, `core/designsystem/preview/` and preview functions at the bottom of files.
- Never hardcode user-facing strings: no `Text("…")` and no `text` / `title` / `label` / `message` / `placeholder` / `contentDescription = "…"` outside preview functions. Log messages, submit keys and test tags are not user-facing and may be literals.
- Light mode only; do not add a dark theme. Token values are placeholders until Figma (PDR-002); change them only in `theme/` and only after an impact analysis.
- Map domain statuses to `StatusTone` (`Neutral`, `Info`, `Success`, `Warning`, `Danger`) in the feature, not in the design system.

## Components

- Reuse components in `core/designsystem/component/<group>/`, `core/designsystem/state/` and `core/ui/state/` before creating new ones; build new shared components with the `build-ui-component` skill.
- Component signature: required params, then `modifier: Modifier = Modifier`, then optional params; stateless (`value` + `onValueChange`); `enabled: Boolean = true`.
- Interactive components accept `interactionSource: MutableInteractionSource? = null` and derive pressed/focused visuals with `val source = interactionSource ?: remember { MutableInteractionSource() }` then `rememberInteractionVisuals(source)`.
- Keep touch targets at least `AppTheme.sizes.minTouchTarget`.
- Get strings via `stringResource(R.string.…)` and `UiText.asString()`; content descriptions come from resources too.

## Previews

- Every public composable has previews at the bottom of its file; preview functions are `private`.
- Annotate component previews with `@ComponentPreviews` and screen previews with `@ScreenPreviews`; wrap each in `PreviewSurface { }`.
- Preview every variant and state (enabled, disabled, pressed, focused, loading, error, empty, as applicable).
- Show pressed/focused with `PreviewSurface(forcedInteraction = ForcedInteraction.Pressed)` / `ForcedInteraction.Focused`.
- Include long and translated samples from `PreviewData`.

## Long content

- Names use `maxLines` + `TextOverflow.Ellipsis`; prices are never truncated (measure the price first, the name takes the remaining width).
- Addresses wrap up to 3 lines.
- Buttons and chips grow in height instead of truncating labels.
- Verify at font scale 1.0, 1.5 and 2.0 and with the `en-XA` pseudo-locale.

## Adaptive layout

- Read layout info with `rememberAdaptiveInfo()`; do not compute window sizes yourself.
- Use two-pane layouts when `usesTwoPane` (Medium/Expanded width); single pane on Compact.
- Size card grids with `cardColumns`.
- Cap widths with `widthIn(max = AppTheme.sizes.formMaxWidth / dialogMaxWidth / contentMaxWidth)`.
- Tablet layouts must also work in portrait and multi-window (Android 16 may ignore the landscape lock).

## Check

- `scripts/ai-hooks/design-lint-check.sh <file-or-dir>` must print nothing before you finish.
